The '''Alcántara Corporation''' ({{Lang-bl|Sociedat Alcántara}}; from [[W:Arabic language|Bayani]] ''al-qantara'' القنطرة, {{Literal translation|the bridge}}) is a Baliscan {{W|worker cooperative}} {{W|cooperative federation|federation}} operating worldwide in {{W|rail transport}} markets, active in the fields of {{W|passenger train|passenger}} and {{W|Freight train|freight transportation}}, signaling and locomotives, with products including the [[Fènix (train)|Fènix]] and [[Halcón (train)|Halcón]] high-speed trains, in addition to suburban, regional and metro trains, as well as trams. Additionally, through the [[Institute of Technical Railway Research|Instituto Investigación Técnica Ferroviaria]], Alcántara conducts research on everything related to trains, railways and their operation.

It is funded by a combination public funding and profits from the sale of it's products both overseas. It works both on developing and 3testing new railway technology, such as {{W|magnetic levitation}}, and on improving the safety and economy of current technology. Its research areas include earthquake detection and alarm systems, obstacle detection on level crossings, improving adhesion between train wheels and tracks, reducing energy usage, noise barriers and preventing vibrations.

